00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.480
<b>EEK</b>

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.990
I'm so sorry!

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:50.030
Be honest. Didn't you ever 
feel like it was too much?

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:53.990
<b>Tea Lessons</b>

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:53.990
Selling in the shop wasn't enough, you had 
to go learn tea ceremony on top of it.

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:57.740
Not at all. It's fun. And I haven't 
studied anything in a long time.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.200
Tea ceremony really is lovely.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.510
It sort of cuts you free from 
the regular perception of time,

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.710
so you feel it passing differently.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.210
It makes me glad I came here.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.970
Now that I think about it... Kanoko-san, 
why did you come to Kyoto?

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:15.660
Does it have some special 
meaning for you or something?

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.220
Oh, um...

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.400
Well...

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.610
And what are you trying to do, 
asking all those questions?

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:22.700
You're right.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:25.290
Don't mind us, Kanoko-san.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:36.860
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:04.760
<b>Chestnut Retrospective</b>

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.820
<i>Why did you come to Kyoto?</i>

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:18.900
Ayu?

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:23.970
<b>How are you?
Are you used to Kyoto now?
\hI hope you can clear up the misunderstanding
\h with Nagomu-san quickly.
\h\hI'll text you again!</b>

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:25.220
<b>Ayu</b>

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.220
<b>Are you used to Kyoto now?
\hI hope you can clear up the misunderstanding
\h with Nagomu-san quickly.
\h\hI'll text you again!</b>

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.220
<b>I'm good!</b>

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.490
Nagomu...

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.610
I'm going home to make wagashi.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.610
I'm the only one who can carry on the shop.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:43.860
Kanoko! Come with me to my parents...

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:45.930
Huh?

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:51.300
I'm sorry.

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:55.460
I like Western sweets.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.570
Bye-bye.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:04.730
<i>Back then, being stubborn and 
contrary was all I could do.</i>

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.550
<i>I thought he'd reconsider it for me.</i>

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.260
<i>Nagomu...</i>

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:21.030
<i>How many glasses did I have?</i>

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.890
<i>I can't remember...</i>

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.440
Oh man. I feel all wobbly.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:28.910
Oh. You too, miss?

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:33.630
Me too!

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:34.920
Nagomu!

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.880
Sorry about that!

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.010
You always start pestering people right away!

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:42.790
Oh, it's fine, isn't it?

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.370
<i>Can't make it, huh?</i>

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.300
Wa... Wa...

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.640
Here. Water.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.700
There's a vending machine over there.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.700
<b>Moonlight Water</b>

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:14.460
<b>Shinjuku Station</b>

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:14.460
<b>Shinjuku Station East Entrance</b>

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.610
Can you get home on your own?

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:18.390
I'm sorry. You were with 
your friends, but now...

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.840
It's not a problem.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:25.150
More importantly, you shouldn't 
drink until you're that unsteady.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:27.500
You're a girl, so it can 
be dangerous, you know?

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:28.440
Well, bye.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.180
I...

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.740
I'd like to thank you somehow.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.480
Don't worry about it. It was
 just a bottle of water.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:39.800
No. You helped me to the bathroom 
and waited until I felt better.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.590
I owe you entirely too much.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.480
Then, next time we meet, 
treat me to tea or something.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.880
Huh? When we meet?

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.320
Only if you remember. Don't worry!

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.250
Oh!

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:00.330
Could it be...

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:01.980
You're the one from back then?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.840
I'll treat you! I promised, after all!

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:08.840
You're the one who's a customer here.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:09.840
Oh.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:16.850
<b>Chestnut</b>

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:16.850
<b>Chestnut</b>

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:15.310
I'm in a band. Back then, we were 
on our way home from practice.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.260
I'll go see your next live concert.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:17.800
For real?

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:18.910
I promise!

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:21.350
You really like promises, don't you?

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.110
We are Chestnut Manju!

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:49.310
Kanoko-chan, should I get you another drink?

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:50.570
Oh, um...

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:51.760
Stop, stop.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.760
That's your fourth, right? 
You should probably leave it there.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:56.760
You promised, right?

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.630
Is it almost the end of the year already?

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.820
Nagomu, you're not going home?

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:38.990
No. It's no big deal.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:43.640
<i>But it doesn't seem like he hates his parents...</i>

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:47.270
<i>He seems happy for some reason.</i>

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:50.150
<i>But if that's true, that's fine.</i>

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:53.660
<i>After all, Nagomu has his band,
 and he has his dreams.</i>

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.410
<i>And he has me. But...</i>

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.420
<i>I wanted to believe</i>

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.070
<i>he'd see me as more 
important than that decision.</i>

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:05.880
<b>To Kanoko
\h I'm sorry</b>

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:04.390
<i>I wanted to flatter myself
 with that thought.</i>

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:21.180
<i>"I'll probably never see him again." 
At least, that's what I thought.</i>

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:24.650
I managed to keep my promise.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:25.880
You remembered?

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:27.690
Of course I did!

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:33.270
<i>Honestly, I...</i>

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:37.750
<i>I seem to really love making 
promises with Nagomu.</i>

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.590
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.590
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:57.500
<i>I wanted to be near Nagomu again, so I came
 to Kyoto. And that's well enough.</i>

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:01.740
<i>But that's just me and my own feelings.</i>

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:03.600
Thank you!

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.530
Oh, Kanoko-san!

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:12.440
I, um, I only had tea lessons today, 
and the rest of the day off,

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.110
so I thought I might buy 
myself something sweet.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:17.620
O-Or something.

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:19.350
In that case...

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:24.620
Wow! A jack-o'-lantern-shaped
 premier namagashi!

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:28.750
Well, it's almost Halloween, so we
 make things like these, too.

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:31.340
Oh, Halloween, is it?

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:33.900
Itsuka-chan, does your 
school do anything for it?

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:34.380
Yes.

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:37.930
Last year, they got capes and 
pointy hats ready for us,

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.510
and my whole class dressed 
as witches together.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:43.100
Wow, I wish I could have seen that.

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:45.690
Do you have a party or anything?

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:50.610
No. But while the pumpkin posters 
are up, we can get candy.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:55.370
The school has the PTA put up the posters.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:58.440
Lately, people do all kinds of 
things for the holiday, don't they?

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:02.000
Then, on the day of Halloween, 
you and the others dress up, and...

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.330
Oh, no, we don't.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:08.000
The children dressing in costumes 
is more than enough already.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.500
Mom, do you know where my chestnut is?

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.670
Oh. Kanoko.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.200
Chestnut? What are you talking about?

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.720
Chestnut? You mean the 
one you put on your head?

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:17.880
Yeah, that one.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:22.300
<b>Itsuka Fight!</b>

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.180
<b>Itsuka Fight!</b>

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:24.180
You can do it!

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:26.740
Yeah!

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:31.930
I clearly remember you wearing 
it for the sports festival.

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:33.690
That's right! The sports festival!

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:35.450
What do you want with that thing, anyway?

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:37.400
I thought I'd wear it for Halloween.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.040
Ugh.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.540
What do you mean, "Ugh"?

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:42.780
It might have gotten caught up in things 
when they were packing up the tent.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:44.170
Packing up?

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:49.540
<b>Colorful
Autumn
 Wagashi</b>

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:47.700
When Itsuka's mother came, 
and I got that phone call.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.510
What did you say?

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:54.200
Oh, what should we do?

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:56.420
For now, I'll come back before everyone else.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.540
What is it? Something wrong?

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.520
Well...

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.380
What should I do with this?

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.100
I'll go check and come back!

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.270
When we were together,

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:22.490
his guitar and chestnut were so important 
he never let me touch them. And now...

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.990
Maybe he's more relaxed 
because he's back home.

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:28.440
He's such an idiot.

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:37.180
If you mean that chestnut, 
we didn't know who it belonged to,

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:40.010
so I was told to leave it in
 the meeting hall.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:45.450
I put it in the storage room.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:48.570
Oh, I'm so glad you found it!

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:50.490
So, it was yours, Nagomu-chan?

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:54.180
Now I'll have my costume 
ready in time for Halloween!

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:59.200
Hmm, that's strange...

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.780
I'm sure it was...

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.500
around here...

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:11.530
It's gone?

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:14.200
I mean... I don't know why.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:18.390
W-Wait just a moment, okay? I'll try
 asking the neighborhood chair.

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:20.760
<b>Held with the Neighborhood Association

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:24.860
They were sorting out what 
was needed and what wasn't,

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:27.690
so one of the sellers might have taken it.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:28.930
One of the sellers?!

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:34.320
Welcome.

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.190
Nagomu-san, what's wrong?

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:40.490
What happened to Nagomu-san?

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:43.350
It seems he still hasn't found 
the thing he's looking for.

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:45.200
The thing he's looking for?

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.700
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.700
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:54.710
<b>[Missing] I've lost something precious to me.
It's still possible that a secondhand goods seller
 has it, but if you see it, please contact me.</b>

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.710
<b>It's this kind of</b>

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:54.960
<b>Post</b>

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.210
<b>chestnut</b>

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.210
<b>chest nut</b>

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.210
<b>CHESTNUT</b>

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.210
<b>chestnut tree</b>

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.210
<b>chestnut dessert</b>

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.210
<b>chestnut pudding</b>

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.210
<b>chestnuts roasting</b>

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.460
Okay.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:59.960
I don't think asking around on 
social media will help you find it.

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:02.710
It's a totally local thing anyway.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:05.130
But there's a chance, right?

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:08.190
Is it really that hard to just let it go?

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:09.390
Well...

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:11.890
I at least want to put up a fight.

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:17.730
Just like the an inside a manju, it's packed
 with all kinds of precious things.

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:21.900
So...

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.760
Why a chestnut, anyway?

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:26.960
Everyone in the band wore them, right?

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.740
It was around this time 
of year back then, too.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:35.750
<b>Nagomu

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.800
We'd only just formed the band,

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:36.500
and we were all saying we needed to 
decide on a name, so we got together.

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:39.740
Hey, sorry I'm late.

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:42.800
What? You've got no taste at all
 when it comes to names!

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.750
Then you come up with something!

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.050
<b>Winds of Enoshima</b>

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:46.050
If I could have, I would have!

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:47.610
Then what's wrong with these?

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:49.680
We need to push harder!

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.560
I'm starting fresh with you guys.

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.420
I don't want to compromise here!

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:57.520
Okay, okay, okay!

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.770
Let's take a break!

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:04.280
<b><i>Chiitara</i></b>

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:04.280
<b><i>As a snack or with drinks</i></b>

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:04.280
So... why are there manju here?

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:08.000
I spotted them near the register and 
bought them before I'd realized it.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.190
Oh, right. I mean, it is fall.

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:13.850
Speaking of chestnut manju, in a 
manga I read a long time ago...

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:16.520
the main character wanted to 
eat tons of chestnut manju,

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:19.000
so he used a mysterious 
object to make more of them.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:22.160
In the end, he created so many, 
he couldn't eat them all.

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:25.920
And if nothing was done, the whole world 
would be buried in chestnut manju.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.840
So he sent them to space with a rocket!

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:32.910
I know that story!

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:33.820
Me too!

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:37.030
That story's actually how 
I found out about chestnut manju!

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:42.440
Those chestnut manju... I wonder 
if they kept multiplying in space.

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:44.320
I know!

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:47.950
Why don't we name our band Chestnut Manju?!

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:51.450
Chestnut manju might 
take over the universe!

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:54.410
They're overflowing with magnificent 
dreams and romance, don't you think?

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:55.980
Whoa. I think I like it!

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:57.660
I'm starting to feel like it might work.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:00.730
Then what about "Space Chestnut Manju" instead?

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:09.670
So we asked someone we knew and 
had chestnut helmets made for us.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:14.010
That chestnut is a memento 
from when we formed the band,

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:16.900
and it's a symbol of the band itself.

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:20.330
Lots of stuff happened and we broke up,

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:23.370
but what we felt back 
then was the real thing.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:26.790
Do you ever...

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:30.330
Do you ever wish you could 
play in a band again?

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:31.450
Not really.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:36.260
I can see something right in front of me 
that I want to follow through to the end.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:39.450
<b>Nagomu

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:44.960
<b>Matsukaze Kanoko</b>

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:49.480
Hey, hello. It's been a while.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.220
<i>Sorry for calling so suddenly.</i>

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:55.450
I heard from my little sister
that you're working in Kyoto.

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:57.370
<i>How is Ayu?</i>

00:15:57.370 --> 00:16:01.140
<i>She texted the other day, 
but I haven't been able to reply yet.</i>

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:05.230
She seems pretty busy lately. 
Don't worry about it.

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:07.080
So, why'd you call today?

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:09.610
Huh? Chestnut?

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:16.410
<i>What's that guy doing, anyway?</i>

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.280
I know, right?

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:21.990
<i>More importantly, Kanoko-chan...</i>

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:23.500
Hm?

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:25.610
<i>Why are you in Kyoto?</i>

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:30.720
<i>It just sort of... turned out this way.</i>

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:33.830
I thought Nagomu must've sent for you.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:39.560
<i>Of course not. Not after he 
left me behind so easily.</i>

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:41.020
Easily, huh?

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:43.480
That's the same as with us.

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:44.380
<i>What?</i>

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:46.520
That guy...

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:52.090
he might think that we said we wanted to 
break up the band out of nowhere, but...

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:55.780
<b>Specialty Matcha
Anmitsu</b>

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:56.280
He'd been worried the whole time,

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.690
worried about his family.

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:01.280
Back when we decided to name 
the band "Chestnut Manju,"

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:04.040
Nagomu was the one who was 
the most excited about it.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:08.870
We thought maybe he wanted to stay 
connected to wagashi however he could.

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:13.530
When Nagomu wasn't around, we all
 talked about it and laughed.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:20.430
The band was fun, but as we thought about
 the future, it felt like time for a change.

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:25.440
We'd planned to take some time and set 
up a place to talk to Nagomu later.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:29.840
<i>"Figure out what your 
priorities really are."</i>

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:31.690
<i>That's what we planned to confront him about.</i>

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:36.440
<i>Then that guy went and traveled 
back to Kyoto on his own.</i>

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:37.430
<i>But...</i>

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:41.900
I think the reason he left the band 
and you, Kanoko-chan, so quickly...

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:43.450
might've been because he didn't want his 
lingering regrets to weaken his resolve.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.810
<i>might've been because he didn't want his 
lingering regrets to weaken his resolve.</i>

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:50.460
<i>But, you know, Kanoko-chan...</i>

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.770
Now that you know your break-up 
was based on a misunderstanding,

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:55.710
couldn't you say you 
want to get back together?

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:57.740
You went all the way to Kyoto.

00:17:57.740 --> 00:18:01.220
<i>It... doesn't feel right to 
say something like that.</i>

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:05.760
<i>Nagomu's changed a lot 
since he came to Kyoto.</i>

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:08.340
<i>But I'm just the same as I was back then.</i>

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:14.430
<i>I think that Nagomu may 
look like he's changed,</i>

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:16.280
<i>but he probably hasn't, really.</i>

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:19.490
It's because of the time 
Nagomu spent with us

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:21.860
that he is who he is now, right?

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:26.890
Maybe you're just seeing him 
take on a bunch of changes.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:31.000
Whether it's in Tokyo or in Kyoto...

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:33.630
when fall comes, the leaves change 
color all the same, right?

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.020
<i>when fall comes, the leaves change 
color all the same, right?</i>

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:40.600
<i>That's what Nagomu did.</i>

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:43.900
<i>What will you do, Kanoko-chan?</i>

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:49.600
<b>Held with the Neighborhood Association

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:56.610
It's Itsuka-chan. Over here!

00:18:58.710 --> 00:18:59.860
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:02.700
You're a cute catgirl!

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.260
Mako-chan, you look good as a vampire.

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.950
Um...

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:08.870
I'm a kurobouzu.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:11.610
Also called an umibouzu. They sink ships.

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:15.040
I even have a bottomless ladle.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:17.010
Sorry. It's hard to tell right away.

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:19.670
Oh! Look!

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:22.330
Wow! It's so realistic!

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:22.330
Isn't that super well made?

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:24.500
That chestnut is huge!

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:25.620
I wonder what kind of yokai she is.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:28.940
Thank you for your hard work!

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:33.020
<b>Keep Upright!</b>

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:33.020
<b><i>Mikan</i></b>

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:33.020
What is all this?

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:35.520
<i>This chestnut?</i>

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:39.530
<i>My grandma lent it to me. She said there 
was a good one in the meeting hall.</i>

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:43.030
<i>Trade for your cat ears? Sure!</i>

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:46.280
Nagomu-san!

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:49.290
Hey, Itsuka!

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:52.290
The chestnut! I found—

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:56.680
Itsuka! Are you all—

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:01.590
Huh?

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:05.850
Hm?

00:20:07.670 --> 00:20:11.380
<i>Chestnut manju might 
take over the universe!</i>

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:18.040
<i>They're overflowing with magnificent 
dreams and romance, don't you think?</i>

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:24.070
Into someone's yard?!

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.930
Other than your hands, are you all right?

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:31.580
Yes. I'm fine.

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:34.060
Thanks for the chestnut.

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.580
It's nothing. I just happened to find it.

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:39.310
I was just about to go give this out.

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:42.460
This is Halloween candy. 
Go and eat it with everyone.

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:43.840
Thank you!

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:46.090
Well, I'll head back now.

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.940
Okay. Be careful.

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:53.310
Oh!

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:53.960
Hm?

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:56.620
I heard you called Takumi about the chestnut.

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.360
Huh? Yeah.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:20:59.820
<b>Sasaki
 What are you doing?

00:20:58.360 --> 00:20:59.900
Thanks.

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:02.860
It looks like everyone checked out my post.

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:02.860
<b>Sasaki
 Everyone seems to be doing well.

00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:06.800
I never imagined we'd meet up again this way.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:09.240
They said they'd be able 
to post pics right away.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:11.830
<b>Nagomu
 What about you guys? You have yours?

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:11.830
I don't even know where to 
start with poking fun at them.

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:14.410
Hold on a sec.

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:22.060
Here are some real chestnut manju.

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:25.230
For me?

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:27.300
As thanks for helping me 
reunite with everyone.

00:21:27.690 --> 00:21:30.440
If you don't want it, give it 
to the mistress of Kafuuen.

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:34.810
I know you like Western sweets better, but...

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:40.170
U-Um... you know!

00:21:40.170 --> 00:21:41.210
I...

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:44.940
I like wagashi, too!

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:47.400
That's all.

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:50.700
Really?

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.030
I'm glad.

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:05.720
Yes...

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:07.960
It's delicious.

00:23:41.360 --> 00:23:43.220
What is all this?

00:23:43.640 --> 00:23:45.720
Let's pretend we didn't see it.

00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:47.240
Yes, let's do that.

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:49.990
<b>To Nagomu
 Make sure you give it back!! 
I hope you find yours soon</b>

00:23:49.990 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:49.990 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>"Long-Awaited Warmth of Spring"</b>

00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:53.050
I was just thinking that I didn't 
know your birthday, Itsuka-chan.

00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:55.320
It's Nagomu's birthday, right?

00:23:56.510 --> 00:23:57.580
All right.

00:23:57.580 --> 00:23:58.740
It's a promise.

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:03.040
This is Japan!

00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:05.960
Is your work going all right?

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:07.880
You don't have to worry about that.

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:10.010
After all, I promised you, Itsuka.
